# What the drives refuse, in strerror's words (roadmap os-server.md P9): a
# missing name, a directory read as a file, a file as a directory, a name
# FAT cannot hold, one past 8.3, a drive that is not there.
program: sh
keys: ls nothing; cat c:/docs; ls c:/readme.txt/x\n
keys: cat a:bad*name; cat a:toolongname.txt; ls /q\n
---
rx286, test build
/mnt/rx286$ ls nothing; cat c:/docs; ls c:/readme.txt/x
nothing: no such file or directory
c:/docs: is a directory
c:/readme.txt/x: not a directory
/mnt/rx286$ cat a:bad*name; cat a:toolongname.txt; ls /q
a:bad*name: invalid argument
a:toolongname.txt: name too long
/q: no such file or directory
/mnt/rx286$
